  "prefLabel": "Ed 1120.01 Applicability; Transfer of Rights",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1120.01 Applicability; Transfer of Rights.\n\n(a) All of the rights and guarantees delineated in Ed 1120 shall apply to parents, adult students, and public agencies, which include LEAs.\n\n(b) The rights of parents under Ed 1100 shall be transferred to children with disabilities who are emancipated minors or who have attained the age of 18 years and have not been adjudicated incompetent consistent with the provisions of 34 CFR 300.320(c) and 34 CFR 300.520.\n\n(c) A parent, as defined in Ed 1102.04(h), or an adult student may authorize an individual to act on their behalf pursuant to a duly executed power of attorney.\n\nSource. (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ed 1100) #9197, eff 6-28-08; ss by #12141, eff 3-24-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html"
